{
	"name": "Mandrake",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/consumables/vegetable/root-potato-leafy-brown.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>This bizarre member of dragonkind bears more resemblance to a root vegetable such as a carrot or parsnip than to a mighty beast of magical prowess. Despite its unusual shape, mandrakes are, in fact, dragons that frequently bury themselves in loose, fertile soil—such as a farmer’s garden. In addition to offering some measure of protection for said farmer’s crops, mandrakes also tend to hoard helpful medicinals. Adventurers who happen upon a mandrake may attempt a DC 14 Persuasion check to convince the dragon to part with a piece of its hoard. On a success, the adventurer receives one of the following: @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-adventuring-gear.Item.1wsowojgg8hcd5wi]{Dried Yewclaw Bark}, @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-adventuring-gear.Item.ktsrqn3m6ifjry80]{Fairy Cap}, @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-adventuring-gear.Item.ufyph3rlho818mv2]{Ironwood Acorn}, or @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-adventuring-gear.Item.cd4i6cm0e8y35iso]{Pressed Spiderbulb}.</p>",
